1
00:04:38,399 --> 00:04:44,399
Better late than never.

2
00:09:16,799 --> 00:09:22,799
The 40 Year Old Virgin is a comedy, romance film directed by Judd Apatow.

3
00:13:55,199 --> 00:14:01,199
Andy Stitzer has a pleasant life with a nice apartment and a
job stamping invoices at an electronics store.

4
00:18:33,599 --> 00:18:39,599
But at age 40, there's one thing Andy hasn't done, and it's really bothering
his sex-obsessed male co-workers: Andy is still a virgin.

5
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:18,000
Determined to help Andy get laid, the guys make it
their mission to de-virginize him.

6
00:27:50,399 --> 00:27:56,399
But it all seems hopeless until Andy meets small
business owner Trish, a single mom.

7
00:32:28,799 --> 00:32:34,799
Andy Stitzer, played by Steve Carell.

8
00:37:07,199 --> 00:37:13,199
Trish Piedmont, played by Catherine Keener.

9
00:41:45,599 --> 00:41:51,599
David, played by Paul Rudd.

10
00:46:24,000 --> 00:46:30,000
Jay, played by Romany Malco.

11
00:51:02,399 --> 00:51:08,399
Cal, played by Seth Rogen.

12
00:55:40,799 --> 00:55:46,799
Beth, played by Elizabeth Banks.

13
01:00:19,199 --> 01:00:25,199
The 40-Year-Old Virgin is a 2005 American romantic comedy film directed by Judd Apatow (in his feature
directorial debut), who produced the film with Clayton Townsend and Shauna Robertson.

14
01:04:57,599 --> 01:05:03,599
It features Steve Carell as the titular 40-year-old virgin
Andy, an employee at an electronics store.

15
01:09:36,000 --> 01:09:42,000
Paul Rudd, Romany Malco, and Seth Rogen play co-workers who resolve to help him lose his
virginity, and Catherine Keener stars as Andy's love interest, Trish.

16
01:14:14,399 --> 01:14:20,399
Watching Carell's performance in Anchorman: The Legend of Ron Burgundy (2004) inspired Apatow to cast
him in the lead role for the film, and they wrote The 40-Year-Old Virgin together.

17
01:18:52,799 --> 01:18:58,799
It was based on a sketch Carell created with The Second
City where a man aged 40 hides a secret.

18
01:23:31,199 --> 01:23:37,199
Filming took place in Los Angeles and San Fernando Valley,
California, from January to April 2005.

19
01:28:09,599 --> 01:28:15,599
The film was released theatrically in the United States on August 19, 2005, by Universal
Pictures, and grossed over $177 million worldwide on a $26 million budget.

20
01:32:48,000 --> 01:32:54,000
Critical reviews were generally positive, with praise for Carell's performance and the film's well-meaning
yet bawdy humor, which was a point of contention by some conservative commentators as well.

21
01:37:26,399 --> 01:37:32,399
He won accolades from the Golden Schmoes Awards and MTV Movie & TV Awards for his role while Keener
received awards from the Boston Society of Film Critics and Los Angeles Film Critics Association.

22
01:42:04,799 --> 01:42:10,799
The 40-Year-Old Virgin was named by the American Film
Institute one of 2005's Top 10 Films.

23
01:46:43,199 --> 01:46:49,199
The film explores themes of first time, virgin, male
friendship, co-workers relationship, poker game.

24
01:51:21,599 --> 01:51:27,599
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
